I can’t believe that my son is going to marry a girl like that, Mrs. Ettman thought, clenching her fists under the table. She wasn’t happy with the situation, but she had decided to stop resisting. She knew her husband and son well enough to realize that too much resistance could backfire. She took a deep breath to regain her composure, then looked at Layla with even more geniality and said, “I hope you enjoy your meal, Layla. I made sure to include lots of dishes that you like.”
