Layla had helped him with these tasks.
She felt lucky to be able to spend several days busily occupied like this. It enabled her to forget about the pen she had lost and the note from the duke that she hadn’t responded to. But now the work was done, and she had to return to Arvis. She slowed her pace as she approached the mansion’s
Fortunately, the duke had made no more mention of the matter. Perhaps he hadn’t yet had the opportunity to. He had also been busy for days, and

Phoebe, with whom he had been secretly communicating, had been locked in a cage in the cottage’s backyard.
